## Objective
- Find novel, reportable vulnerabilities in the latest Naver Whale browser (currently v4.39.410.14) focusing on sync flow, Whale-only libraries, and browser core, within program scope rules.

## Important Details
- **Scope**: Latest-version Whale browser bugs, third-party libs used ONLY by Whale (not Chromium), sync bugs. Excludes: `*.naver.com`, `*.navercorp.com`, built-in extension servers (Papago, Belli), URL preview spoofing, XSS Auditor bypass, IETab, SafeBrowsing FP/FN
- **Program rule**: client-side software only; static source analysis + repro-first validation; sha256 only for secrets
- **Desktop version**: v4.39.410.14 (Chromium 138); same-day double release Aug 18 with login-server-error hotfix
- **Android version**: v3.9.14.9 (364.2MB arm64 XAPK, SHA-256 `6f7c7907...`)
- **Binary acquisition**: `repo.whale.naver.com` confirmed accessible (HTTP 200, 166MB .deb); sha256=`10de323e6f89a5195f7e558259e849be75792e021decc2be8e61848b6653ce19` (binary); `6458a95a...` (.deb package)
- **GitHub repo**: `naver/whale-browser-developers` — documentation-only (last commit 2019-09-23), 0 releases, 4 branches (master 3/v2 2/translate 57/jdkim 39 blobs), has_wiki=true; 0 sync/crypto source files exist in any public branch
- **NVD status**: 28 total whale CVEs, 0 published in 2026; latest CVE-2025-69235 @2025-12-30; 8-month disclosure gap confirmed static
- **NVD query**: Use `keywordSearch=whale` (not `naver+whale` which returns 0); `services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cves/2.0` is primary endpoint (nvd.nist.gov/rest Cloudflare-blocked)
- **Sandbox limitations**: cloudfront DNS `No answer` (hard block), APKMirror 403, Uptodown 410, APKPure CDN 403, pstatic 404 — only `repo.whale.naver.com` works
- **Key crypto discovery (Aug 21)**: Epoch-key response parser (`0xc0d5c91`–`0xc0d5eb6`) consumes plain JSON with ZERO crypto-helper calls — no HMAC/MAC/nonce/timestamp verification before epoch-key confirmation
- **WhaleNidAuth pipeline**: `client_private_key`/`session_id`/`csrf_token` arrive as JSON trio via `OnEpochKeyConfirmed` WebUI bridge (`inline_login_handler_impl_whale.cc`); HMAC signing uses `ECDH(PKCS#8 client_private_key, hex server pubkey)` domain-separated `whale:hmac:`+`v1`, binds `X-CSRF-Token`/`X-Timestamp`/`X-Nonce` — request-side only
- **WBC crypto layer**: `wbc.cc` + `wbc_wrapper_apis.cc` + `encryptor.cc` compiled into binary; separate from Chromium `os_crypt/sync/`
- **9 Whale-specific sync source files** in binary: `whale_sync_auth_manager.cc`, `trusted_vault_request_whale.cc`, `sync_service_impl_whale.cc`, `sync_stopped_reporter_whale.cc`, `data_type_worker_whale.cc`, `sync_server_connection_manager_whale.cc`, `whale_sync_util.cc`, plus 2 more under `whale/components/sync/`
- **OSCrypt coexistence**: Chromium 138 async OSCrypt + legacy Whale fork both present
- **Rejected classes**: sidebar/dual-tab/web-panel SOP-CSP bypass (dup CVE-2025-69234/69235), socket.io event-handler injection (conf 38), installer DLL search-order regression (conf 50), sidebar SOP bypass (conf 32<40)
- **KDF debug string**: `%s: kdf key len: %d` proven to be libsrtp/WebRTC, NOT sync-crypto
- **authkey_fetcher fork**: `whale/components/signin/public/identity_manager/authkey_fetcher.cc` confirmed as Whale fork inside upstream identity_manager
- **utilityPrivate API**: `setSyncEncryptionKeys`, `getSyncCacheGuid`, `getPushServerURL`, `showLoginPopup` with origin-binding gaps

